    <name>Social Media Marketing</name>
    <intro>&lt;h5&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Types%20of%20Communication%20-%20%20Social%20Media%20%282%29.png" alt="" width="1575" height="300"&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" style="float: left; padding-right: 10px;" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Social%20Media.png?time=1741203147093" alt="" width="100" height="100"&gt;Information about how we use social media to spread the good work happening in the department and around the state.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;</intro>
    <introformat>1</introformat>
    <content>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Types%20of%20Communication%20-%20%20Social%20Media.png" alt="" width="1575" height="300"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Maine DOE uses social media for broad audiences and for a variety or purposes, which include promoting Newsroom posts, good news, recognition and celebration events, professional opportunities, and a host of other areas of focus. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting platforms: &lt;/strong&gt;The department primarily posts on &lt;em&gt;Facebook, LinkedIn, Instagram, and YouTube.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Maine%20DOE%20Facebook%20Icon%20%28Dark%29.png" alt="" width="150" height="150"&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Maine%20DOE%20LinkedIn%20Icon%20%28Dark%29.png" alt="" width="150" height="150"&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Maine%20DOE%20Instagram%20Icon%20%28Dark%29.png" alt="" width="150" height="150"&gt;&lt;img class="img-fluid" role="presentation" src="@@PLUGINFILE@@/Maine%20DOE%20YouTube%20Icon%20%28Dark%29.png" alt="" width="150" height="150"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facebook&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://www.facebook.com/MaineDepartmentofEducation1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;@MaineDepartmentofEducation1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/education-maine-department-of" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;@Education-Maine-Department-Of&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instagram&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://www.instagram.com/mainedepted/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;@mainedepted&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YouTube&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/MaineDOEComm" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;@MaineDOEComm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How do you get your content on social media?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class="TextRun Highlight SCXW27183964 BCX8" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;For &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;Facebook, LinkedIn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;and Instagram&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="TextRun Highlight SCXW27183964 BCX8" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"&gt; &lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;Newsroom articles intended for a broad audience (professional learning, good news, requests for public comment, Maine DOE highlights) will automatically be posted on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt; social media&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt; within a week of being posted in the Maine DOE Newsroom. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;The Communications Team will &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;either use images you provide with the article&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt; (in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;Communications &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;Workflow)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt; or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;generate a graphic for the post using one of our templates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;. If you have other specific posts &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;you’d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt; like to make or want Maine DOE to share &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;the post of a school or partner organization,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8"&gt;reach out to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class="Hyperlink SCXW27183964 BCX8" href="mailto:Rachel.Paling@maine.gov" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"&gt;&lt;span class="TextRun Highlight Underlined SCXW27183964 BCX8" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="none"&gt;&lt;span class="NormalTextRun SCXW27183964 BCX8" data-ccp-charstyle="Hyperlink"&gt;Rachel.Paling@maine.gov&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;span class="EOP SCXW27183964 BCX8" data-ccp-props="{&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720}"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For YouTube, fill out the &lt;a href="https://forms.office.com/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=q6g_QX0gYkubzeoajy-GTo9TTqa8VhVMnzxeeWJViwtUNFFMUDZTV1lBOTcwTklYMDI4VkpFR0NVWS4u" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;YouTube Request Form&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your video cannot contain copyrighted images or audio that you do not have permission to use. Uploading these to YouTube can result in a copyright strike and lead to the department permanently losing our YouTube channel. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Check out our latest YouTube videos!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;script src="https://apps.elfsight.com/p/platform.js" defer="defer"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
